@startuml spawn-with-user
!theme plain
' Updated: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); user-manager ownership of stop made explicit
title Spawn through the dispatcher (v1.3): grant check without amplification, capacity, OS user, key, launch, result, retire

participant "Orchestrator\n(OS user orch_a)" as O
participant "Launch dispatcher" as D
participant "Trust\n(grants, revocation)" as T
participant "Capacity (S3)" as Cap
participant "User manager / helper\n(sudo)" as PH
participant "Key keeper" as KK
participant "Launcher\n(curator run)" as L
participant "Credential broker" as CB
participant "Session host" as SH
participant "Bridge" as BR
participant "Worker\n(OS user w_17)" as W
participant "Task core\n(board)" as B

O -> D: dispatch(LaunchRequest{request_id, role developer, profile+pin,\nmode headless, io thread, grants requested for the child})
D -> T: granted(orch_a, spawn.role developer, project P)?\nrequested child grants ⊆ delegable grants of orch_a?
alt not granted or amplification
  T --> D: refused{grant | amplification}
  D --> O: refused
else granted
  T --> D: ok
  D -> Cap: admit_host(local, job_class)
  alt no slot or a gate refuses
    Cap --> D: queued{handle} | refused{gate}
    D --> O: queued | refused
  else lease
    D -> PH: create user w_17: private home 0700 under the agents tree, no parent ACL,\nfirewall: only its own listener of the bound profile, model-provider endpoints only (F-27; owner 2026-10-13)
    PH --> D: uid, account generation
    D -> KK: register (uid, generation, identity path, owner, registration generation);\nrecord one-shot flag (API unpublished; dispatcher §14 gate)
    KK --> D: public key + root signature (registry record)
    D -> T: bind role developer -> identity w_17 for project P\n(signed by the dispatcher under the owner's delegable grant)
    D -> L: caller-side compose-only plan, expect_pin for admitted worker
    L -> SH: intake; fence closed
    SH -> D: host_start under admitted permit (jointly gated)
    D -> PH: invoke approved privileged launcher with immutable plan
    PH -> W: drop UID; start admitted agent-side executor/holder
    W -> CB: re-resolve protected binding; fresh broker connection after UID drop
    CB --> W: lease material for this admitted launch only (D-EXECUTOR)
    L -> BR: bind(thread, audience); mailbox for w_17
    SH -> SH: token, readiness, fence open
    SH --> D: RUN{request_id, identity w_17, execution}
    D --> O: RunHandle (RUN record kept by the dispatcher)
    D -> B: RUN attached to the element (reconciliation)
  end
end

== result ==
W -> BR: post result (binding grant); keeper signs
BR -> B: outcome proposal (B5)
B -> B: accept or refuse; review by the playbook

== retire ==
D -> PH: journaled exec.stop; latest receipt; account-wide absence
PH --> D: confirmed account-wide process absence before retirement proceeds
D -> PH: delete home (only the service-generated metadata export is kept, F-1),\ndelete user w_17, remove firewall rules last
D -> KK: detach active registration before UID reuse
opt registered one-shot flag, same registering dispatcher, retirement confirmed
  D -> KK: separate journaled identity revocation (same effect on retry)
end
note over D, KK: Standing identity survives retirement; operator-signed revocation only
D -> T: revocation snapshot refreshed
@enduml
